ptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/ezyang/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"I was investigating the comment chain over in https://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/pull/25595#discussion_r322455893, and ran into a bug.\r\n\r\nTo reproduce, you need to get rid of multiple dispatch for multinomial and call it, e.g.:\r\n```\r\ntorch.multinomial(torch.rand(2,3, device='cuda'), 5, True, out=torch.randn(2,3, device='cuda').long())\r\n```\r\n\r\nYou'll get an error like:\r\n```\r\nUnrecognized tensor type ID: VariableTypeId\r\n```\r\n\r\nwhat's happening here is we are trying to pass a variable to a method that only accepts tensors, and this is already checked with a reasonable error message:\r\nhttps://github.com/pytorch/pytorch/blob/16605ef2ebbc1fca3b2d5292591a4c72d42df34c/aten/src/ATen/Utils.h#L74-L77\r\n\r\nbut the first call of `tensorTypeIdToBackend(impl::dispatchTypeId(expr.type_set())` bails before we get there.","closed_by":{"login":"facebook-github-bot","id":6422482,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjY0MjI0ODI=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/6422482?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/facebook-github-bot","html_url":"https://github.com/facebook-github-bot","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/facebook-github-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/facebook-github-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/facebook-github-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/face